.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.I Encode
and
.I decode
answer a codec
.B Error
when the bytes are wrong: a size that disagrees with the buffer, a
string past the 16-bit length a length prefix can hold, a walk of more
than sixteen elements, or a type byte that names no message.
A protocol failure, the request well-formed and the answer no, is an
.B Errno
inside an
.B Rlerror
reply instead, never a codec
.BR Error .
.SH BUGS
.I Session.next_fid
is a monotonic counter that refuses at its ceiling rather than wrapping,
so a session runs out of fids after four billion opens; there is no free
list yet fed by
.BR Tclunk .
